<?php declare(strict_types=1); ?><!DOCTYPE html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="UTF-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1.0"><meta name="description" content="Trust-Worthy AI publishes open, adversarial investigations that trace difficult claims to evidence and invite anyone to challenge the findings."><title>Trust-Worthy AI | Open Truth Trials</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="/truth/truth-worthy.css"></head><body><header class="topbar"><div class="wrap nav"><a class="brand" href="/">PROJECT <span>UNVEILED</span></a><nav class="navlinks"><a href="#trials">Truth Trials</a><a href="#ask">Ask a Question</a><a href="/book/research.html">Research Standards</a><a href="/book/">Project Unveiled</a></nav></div></header><main><section class="hero"><div class="wrap"><div class="eyebrow">Trust-Worthy AI · Public Evidence Record</div><h1>Don't trust the answer. Examine the evidence.</h1><p>Hard questions deserve more than canned answers. Trust-Worthy traces claims toward primary evidence, tests provenance and context, searches for counterevidence, attacks its own reasoning, publishes uncertainty, and lets anyone try to overturn the finding.</p><div class="manifesto"><strong>No protected conclusions.</strong> Christianity, skepticism, institutions, Project Unveiled, and Trust-Worthy itself face the same rule: if better evidence wins, the public finding changes.</div></div></section><section class="section" id="trials"><div class="wrap"><div class="eyebrow">Published & Open Investigations</div><h2>Every day, something goes on trial.</h2><div class="grid"><article class="card"><div class="case-head"><div><div class="case-id">TW-CLAIM-000001</div><h2>Does God individually cause or permit every bad thing?</h2></div><div class="status">PROVISIONAL</div></div><p>The evidence does not require the conclusion that every harmful event is individually caused or separately permitted by God. But the opposite absolute—“God is not in control”—also outruns the evidence.</p><div class="finding"><strong>What survived:</strong> the biblical material holds divine sovereignty, human agency, ordinary causation, and hostile spiritual agency in tension rather than reducing every tragedy to one simple mechanism.</div><p><a class="button" href="/truth/case-000001.php">Read the Full Investigation</a></p></article><article class="card"><div class="case-head"><div><div class="case-id">TW-CLAIM-000002</div><h2>Did Jesus teach the modern Romans Road / sinner's prayer?</h2></div><div class="status">NEW</div></div><p>Trust-Worthy puts a familiar evangelical salvation formula on trial: Jesus' recorded teaching, Romans itself, conversion history, and the strongest defense of the modern practice.</p><div class="finding"><strong>First-pass finding:</strong> the standardized method appears to be a later evangelistic framework built from genuine New Testament material—not a formula recorded on Jesus' lips.</div><p><a class="button" href="/truth/case-000002.php">Examine Case 000002</a></p></article></div></div></section><section class="section" id="ask"><div class="wrap grid"><article class="card"><div class="eyebrow">Private Question Intake</div><h2>What question should go on trial?</h2><p class="muted">Submit a question privately. Trust-Worthy reviews it before opening any public investigation. Honest questions are welcome; publication is not automatic.</p><form class="challenge" action="/truth/question-submit.php" method="post"><input type="hidden" name="opened_at" id="questionOpenedAt" value=""><div class="hp" aria-hidden="true"><label>Website<input name="website" tabindex="-1" autocomplete="off"></label></div><div class="row"><div><label for="topic">Topic</label><select id="topic" name="topic" required><option value="">Choose one</option><option value="jesus">Jesus / Gospel</option><option value="doctrine">Doctrine / theology</option><option value="history">History / sources</option><option value="science">Science / nature</option><option value="current-events">Current events</option><option value="other">Other</option></select></div><div><label for="questionName">Name or handle (optional)</label><input id="questionName" name="name" maxlength="100" autocomplete="name"></div></div><label for="question">Your question</label><textarea id="question" name="question" minlength="20" maxlength="3000" required></textarea><label for="context">Why does this matter, or what evidence should be considered? (optional)</label><textarea id="context" name="context" maxlength="2000"></textarea><label for="questionEmail">Email for an update (optional)</label><input id="questionEmail" type="email" name="email" maxlength="190" autocomplete="email"><button class="button" type="submit">Submit a Question for Review</button></form></article><aside class="card"><h3>What happens next</h3><ul class="rules"><li>Your question is stored privately for review.</li><li>We clarify the actual claim before investigating it.</li><li>Public Truth Trials are selected for evidence, scope, and public value—not popularity.</li><li>A published case can be challenged and revised.</li></ul><div class="finding"><strong>Not a debate box.</strong><br>Trust-Worthy investigates questions before it asks anyone to take a side.</div></aside></div></section><section class="section"><div class="wrap grid"><article class="card"><div class="eyebrow">The Method</div><h2>Trust-Worthy investigates before it answers.</h2><div class="steps"><div class="step"><div class="num">1</div><div><strong>Define</strong><span>Separate the actual proposition from assumptions hidden inside the question.</span></div></div><div class="step"><div class="num">2</div><div><strong>Trace</strong><span>Follow citations backward toward primary and earliest accessible evidence.</span></div></div><div class="step"><div class="num">3</div><div><strong>Corroborate</strong><span>Distinguish independent evidence from thousands of repetitions of one source.</span></div></div><div class="step"><div class="num">4</div><div><strong>Attack</strong><span>Build the strongest credible case against the leading explanation.</span></div></div><div class="step"><div class="num">5</div><div><strong>Reason</strong><span>Separate documented evidence, inference, interpretation, and unresolved questions.</span></div></div><div class="step"><div class="num">6</div><div><strong>Publish & revise</strong><span>Every serious challenge can become part of the permanent version history.</span></div></div></div></article><aside class="card"><h3>The Trial Rules</h3><ul class="rules"><li>No third-party fact-check verdict is treated as authority.</li><li>Primary and earliest accessible evidence receives priority.</li><li>Contrary evidence must be actively sought.</li><li>Evidence and interpretation remain visibly separate.</li><li>“We do not know” is a legitimate finding.</li><li>No founder belief receives immunity.</li><li>Successful challenges permanently revise the public case.</li></ul><h3 style="margin-top:28px">Challenge language</h3><div class="labels"><span class="label">Source</span><span class="label">Date</span><span class="label">Translation</span><span class="label">Context</span><span class="label">Logic</span><span class="label">Counterevidence</span><span class="label">Assumption</span></div></aside></div></section></main><footer class="footer"><div class="wrap">Trust-Worthy AI · Project Unveiled · Truth is not afraid of questions.</div></footer><script>document.getElementById("questionOpenedAt").value=Math.floor(Date.now()/1000);</script></body></html>